Orbis: About dialog describes Orbis, without Mozilla's community, donation, terms and privacy links.

community-2 (and community-exp, shown on pre-release versions) said "Orbis is designed by Orbis, a global
community ...", with the vendor name linked to mozilla.org and "global community" to about:credits. Both
descriptions now use a new string, orbis-about-description, with no links; community-2 and community-exp
are deleted. The attribution to Mozilla stays in trademarkInfo (brand.ftl), so it is not repeated. The
"Want to help? Make a donation or get involved!" blurbs (helpus, helpus-referrals2; links to
foundation.mozilla.org, mozilla.org/contribute and about:referrals) are removed, with the aboutDialog.js
code that toggled them and the Referrals import. The "Terms of Use" and "Privacy Notice" links (Mozilla's
documents for Firefox) and their strings are removed; "Licensing Information" stays. See docs/PATCHES.md.

